The system has been transformed into a Pan-Mizoram Village Council Land Pass Management Portal supporting all villages across Mizoram.
Key New Capabilities
Selectable Village System for all Villages in Mizoram:
Village Switcher: Select from preset villages across Mizoram (Saiphai, Bilkhawthlir, Vairengte, Bairabi, Darlawn, Sairang, Khawbung, Hnahthial, Tlabung, etc.) or configure any new village.
Independent Registry per Village: Each village has its own custom Land Pass serial numbers, official seal, letterhead, and bylaws.
User Registration with Role Differentiation:
Village Council Secretary: Administrative role with authority to issue land passes, edit boundaries, manage user permissions, and configure village bylaws.
Citizen User: Free immediate registration in View Mode Only to search village records, verify authenticity via QR code, and download/print certificates.
Mandatory UPI Payment Flow for VC Secretary:
Required Fields: Secretary User Name, Passkey (PIN / Security code), Contact Number, and Village Selection.
Payment Gateway: Integrated UPI payment interface supporting Google Pay, PhonePe, Paytm, and Scan UPI QR Code.
Verification: Generates live UPI payment URI and verifies transaction UTR reference number before completing account creation and elevating user to Council Secretary.
Mandatory Village Profile & Custom Bylaws Update:
Jurisdiction Details: Village Name, RD Block Name, District Name, State Name (Mizoram), and PIN Code.
Custom Serial Prefixes:
Huan Ram Pass Prefix: e.g., MZ-05-SPH-HR- (or SPH/VC/HR/)
In Hmun Pass Prefix: e.g., MZ-05-SPH-IH- (or SPH/VC/IH/)
Photo Picker for Village Council Logo: Upload official council seal or crest image with preview.
Land Pass Conditions & Terms Editor: Multi-line editor to customize village-specific customary land restrictions, obligations, and court bylaws.
Signatories: Customizable President and Secretary names for official authorization.
Dynamic Official A4 Certificate & PDF Archival:
Printable certificate automatically adapts to the selected village's letterhead, official logo, custom pass prefixes, village-specific conditions, and signatories.
