Root Cause Identified & Resolved
Root Cause of Save/Update/Delete Freezes:
The secondary Realtime Database (https://vclandpass.firebaseio.com/) was reporting a downgrade/deactivation by Firebase ("The Firebase database 'vclandpass' has be downgraded by a database owner").
Because await set(...) and await remove(...) were waiting indefinitely for server acknowledgments from that downgraded endpoint, operations in handleSavePass, handleConfirmDeletePass, saveHouseholdRecord, deleteHouseholdRecord, saveTaxRecord, and updateUserStatus were hanging in the background, preventing modal closure and UI state updates.
We removed all blocking await statements on RTDB writes across realtimeSync.ts, ptmsService.ts, userService.ts, villageService.ts, offlineSync.ts, and App.tsx, wrapping them in non-blocking background workers with timeout guards.
Root Cause of Missing Auto-Sync:
The primary Firestore real-time snapshot listeners (onSnapshot) were only configured for land_passes and users. households, property_taxes, and villages were lacking Firestore live listeners.
We added dedicated real-time onSnapshot listeners for:
households (collection(db, 'households'))
property_taxes (collection(db, 'property_taxes'))
villages (collection(db, 'villages'))
land_passes (collection(db, 'land_passes'))
users (collection(db, 'users'))
Any create, update, or delete in any collection now syncs live across all browser tabs and devices in real time.
Firebase Cloud Database & Security Rules:
Verified terms acceptance and reprovisioned ai-studio-saiphaivillageco-86a1f30d-799f-4fef-b2be-ea1fa20a70b9.
Redeployed firestore.rules granting full read/write permissions for all collections (land_passes, households, property_taxes, villages, users, and audit_logs).
